   "subject": "increase space for column labels in gheatmap",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m trying to plot a tree + heatmap but the space available for the column labels is rather limited even with extreme reduction on fontsize and colnames_angle (they are names of phyla, so full words)</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ggtree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tidyverse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>dist </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;dist.csv&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> header </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">names </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>dist1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#View(dist1)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>hc </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> hclust</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dist1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>den </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dendrogram</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggtree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">den</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>mytable </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mytable </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;table.csv&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> header </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">names </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>gheatmap</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mytable</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         low </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;green&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> high </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> color </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;white&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         offset </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">03</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#font.size=2,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         colnames_angle</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         hjust</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         colnames_position </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bottom&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> colnames_offset_y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  geom_tiplab</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">size </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br><br></span></div></code></div><br></div><div>Any idea, how to increase the space available for the column names?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you in advance,</div><div>Xabi<br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "SQLPVLSxAQAJ",
   "from": "jonnations",
