   "subject": "Re: increase space for column labels in gheatmap",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><div dir=\"auto\">Hi Xabier,</div></div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">You could try adding ‘’’+coord_fixed()’’’ to your code. This preserves the aspect ratio. </div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">Then you can save the plot to whatever size you want using:</div><div dir=\"auto\">‘’’output_file=“myfile.pdf”</div><div dir=\"auto\">gg_save(output_file, width = 10, height = 7.5)’’’ </div><div dir=\"auto\">Or whatever width and height numbers are good for you. </div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">Basically your keeping the plot the same size but making the bounding box whatever size you want. This should be one way to solve the problem. I’m sure there are others! </div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
